<p>Israel’s security cabinet has approved new measures to restart and expand land registration in the Israeli-occupied West Bank for the first time since the process was frozen after the 1967 war, while also easing land purchases by Israeli settlers across the territory. Israeli officials said the policy aims to strengthen governance and security, add transparency and enforcement, and counter what the cabinet described as Palestinian Authority-backed “illegal land registration” efforts. Palestinian leaders and several rights-focused voices called the plan a step toward de facto annexation and warned it could speed up settlement expansion and dispossess Palestinians. They point out that much Palestinian land has historically gone unregistered, and formal registration can determine permanent ownership. The decision has drawn international criticism and highlights how land policy remains a key flashpoint, with direct implications for any future Palestinian state envisioned in parts of the West Bank.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/fdYvoRD4oiAXiccg-xWOTWFphqFtsZqo3tKWYrdL4Qs51SivVsB9MgCXkb3iMLbArCrWp5DF0Hg6l_yH8g6zJlla0_mVdzlvuX-1jBU29JDv' alt='Israeli soldiers stand guard during a weekly settlers’ tour in Hebron, in the Israeli-occupied West Bank on February 14, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ministers backing: Several reports say Justice Minister Yariv Levin, Defence Minister Israel Katz and Finance Minister Bezalel Smotrich pushed the proposal, presenting it as a way to tighten Israeli control and advance settlement activity.</li><li>Land title effect: Several outlets note that resuming “settlement of land title” could shift control of wide areas by requiring claimants to come forward during registration periods, potentially affecting who is recognized as the legal owner.</li><li>Registry access and transactions: RT said the cabinet package also repeals a rule dating to Jordanian administration, making land registries public rather than private, alongside steps to facilitate land purchases by Israeli settlers.</li><li>Legal arguments: Critics cited in coverage argue that international law bars an occupying power from confiscating land in occupied territory, while Israeli ministers say the policy improves governance and security.</li><li>Broader tensions: Dawn linked the decision to ongoing violence, including Gaza civil defence reporting that Israeli strikes killed at least 12 people in less than 24 hours despite a truce.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli Defence Minister Israel Katz: Katz described land registration as a security and governance measure intended to ensure Israeli control, enforcement and freedom of action in the West Bank. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/israel-approves-west-bank-land-registration/'>Michael West</a>)</li><li>Israeli Finance Minister Bezalel Smotrich: Smotrich portrayed the decision as part of a “revolution of settlement,” framing it as strengthening Israel’s hold across the territory. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/israel-approves-west-bank-land-registration/'>Michael West</a>)</li><li>Palestinian Authority presidency: The PA presidency rejected the cabinet decision as “a de facto annexation” and a “serious escalation,” arguing it undermines signed agreements and contradicts UN Security Council resolutions. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973604/israel-moves-to-claim-west-bank-land-as-state-property'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Hamas: Hamas condemned the move as an attempt “to steal and Judaise lands” by registering them as “state lands”. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973604/israel-moves-to-claim-west-bank-land-as-state-property'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Israeli rights groups (as cited by Al Jazeera): Israeli rights groups cited by Al Jazeera warned that the registration plan could “systematise dispossession” and further an aim of annexing Palestinian territory. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/16/israels-move-to-register-land-systematises-dispossession-of-palestinians'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-will-begin-contentious-west-bank-land-registration-in-new-step-to-deepen-control/article70636437.ece'>Israel will begin contentious West Bank land registration in new step to deepen control</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/632580-israel-west-bank-land/'>Israel approves major land grab in West Bank</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-government-approves-new-west-bank-land-policy/a-75981876'>Israeli government approves new West Bank land policy</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/israel-approves-west-bank-land-registration/'>Israel approves West Bank land registration</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israels-plan-to-install-west-bank-regulations-denounced-as-illegal-mega-land-grab'>Israel&#x27;s plan to install West Bank regulations denounced as illegal &#x27;mega land grab&#x27;</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Middle-East/2026/0215/israel-west-bank-land-registration'>Israel will begin West Bank land registration in new step to deepen control</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israeli-cabinet-approves-west-bank-land-registration-palestinians-condemn-de-facto-annexation'>Israeli Cabinet approves West Bank land registration, Palestinians condemn ‘de-facto annexation’</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3343652/israel-will-begin-contentious-west-bank-land-registration-new-step-deepen-control'>Israel launches new West Bank land policy seen as a ‘mega land grab’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973604/israel-moves-to-claim-west-bank-land-as-state-property'>Israel moves to claim West Bank land as ‘state property’</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobe